<!--
    The register inputs of an x86-32 callee read off its own code (option
    calleereginputs, default on on x86-32 Windows). Each fixture is decompiled
    twice: `option calleereginputs off` (the bug), then the shipped default.

    x86win.cspec's default model, __stdcall, has no register parameters, so a
    __thiscall call to a function with no declared prototype dropped `this`
    (ECX), and the stack stores the caller had made for its own locals were
    taken as the callee's stack arguments instead.

    thiscall_pe_i386.exe (VC8 /O2 C++, build notes in thiscall_pe_i386.s): use
    (0x401040) constructs a local B (B::B at 0x401020, this = &buf) and calls
    V::len2 on a local V through a `jmp` stub (0x4010a8, this = &v).

    calleereginputs_pe_i386.exe (clean-room asm, notes in
    calleereginputs_pe_i386.asm): calls where the caller's own data flow does
    not show the register is an argument, so an ECX the callee reads must not
    cost the call its stack arguments (#16 pins that none is lost). forward
    passes its own `this` through without touching ECX; inherited loads ECX
    from an ESI it never set; reload pushes p for a __cdecl call and loads the
    pushed slot back as the next call's `this`; drift's stack solution rests on
    guessed pops (an import, a callee whose pop is not applied), and a `this`
    formed past the guess must not alias the import's argument slot;
    fastcaller passes ECX and EDX to a __fastcall callee. partial calls
    low_word after a call that clobbers ECX; low_word sets CX before it copies
    all of ECX, so it reads no register and the call takes only its stack
    argument (#17), not the ECX the earlier call left behind.

    vcall_pe_i386.exe (clean-room, source and recipe in vcall_pe_i386.s): calls
    through the vtable of the object in ECX. vcall (0x401000) is a virtual
    member taking one push; comcall (0x401010) a COM method, which pushes the
    interface as its first argument; reserve (0x401020) a virtual member whose
    `push ecx` only reserves the slot a float store fills; ctable (0x401040)
    a C __cdecl function pointer in a table reached through ECX, cleaned up
    by the caller; comcopy (0x401050) a COM method whose interface is pushed
    from the register ECX was copied from; comesi (0x401060) five COM calls
    through ESI, copied from ECX before the first of them; crosscall
    (0x4010a0) a C table reached through ESI, copied from ECX before a call
    that clobbers ECX. By default the virtual members get their receiver; the
    COM methods keep their pushed interface, once; the C calls get no
    receiver (#26, #27). A last pass with C types (`ctypes`,
    `calltargettype`) types the virtual call's target as a function pointer
    whose first parameter is `this` (#25).
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
